{
  "id": "Compound::DB00363 - Gene::1132",
  "verbalization": "Clozapine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Chrm2, which is a key player in the activation of G-protein coupled receptors, both acetylcholine and neurotransmitter-related. This binding leads to Chrm2 participating in the activation of G-protein coupled receptor activity, which in turn is associated with Chrm4. The evidence suggests that Clozapine may modulate Chrm4 through a mechanism involving Chrm2, potentially influencing receptor activity or signaling pathways. The overlapping roles of Chrm2 in different receptor activities—such as acetylcholine and neurotransmitter receptors—indicate a possible general mechanism of action, where Clozapine may affect multiple receptor pathways through a shared intermediate. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Clozapine and Chrm4, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
